---
import ToolPage from '@versal/ui/ToolPage.astro';

const title = "cURL to Fetch Converter";
const description = "Parse a curl command and generate browser or Node fetch() code using async/await  — methods, headers, JSON bodies, cookies and basic auth included.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How do I convert curl to JavaScript fetch?",
    "answer": "Paste a curl command into the input and click Convert. The tool parses the URL, method, headers, and body, then outputs an equivalent JavaScript fetch() call. Both async/await and Promise.then() styles are available."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does it handle authentication headers?",
    "answer": "Yes. Basic auth, Bearer tokens, API keys in headers, and custom headers are all preserved in the generated fetch code. Form data and JSON bodies are handled appropriately."
  }
];
import ToolNav from '@versal/ui/ToolNav.astro';
import BaseLayout from '@versal/ui/BaseLayout';
---

<ToolPage
  site="codegen"
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://jsonversal.com/codegen/tools/curl-to-fetch/"
  current="/codegen/tools/curl-to-fetch/"
  faqs={faqs}
  about={[
    {
      "heading": "What the generated call actually contains",
      "body": [
        "Output is a bare `fetch(url)` when the parsed command has no method, headers or body, and an options object otherwise. The body appears only when `-d` or a variant was present, and only when it parses as JSON after trimming — the payload is re-serialised through `JSON.stringify`, so key order and number formatting come from a JSON round trip rather than from your text. A `Content-Type: application/json` header is added only when you supplied none, and the output carries a comment marking that the tool made that decision.",
        "Authentication and cookies are folded in. `-u user:pass` becomes an `Authorization: Basic <base64>` header computed from the UTF-8 bytes of the credential, and it is skipped when an `Authorization` header already exists so an explicit bearer token is never overwritten. A `-b` cookie string is appended to an existing `Cookie` header or added as a new one, and header casing is preserved exactly as typed rather than normalized."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Two headers in the output are forbidden to browsers",
      "body": [
        "The Fetch specification designates certain names as forbidden header names, and the browser strips them from the request before it leaves. `User-Agent` is the important one: curl's `-A` has no client-side equivalent in a page, because a script cannot set it and the browser replaces it with its own value. `Cookie` is on the same list — setting it from `fetch` is ignored, which means the merged `Cookie` header in generated code is effectively documentation of what curl would have sent, not something a page can actually deliver.",
        "Credentials are governed separately. `credentials` defaults to `same-origin`, so a cross-origin request drops cookies and any `Authorization`-derived session silently, and you need `credentials: 'include'` plus a matching `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials` header and a specific origin rather than a wildcard. That option is not emitted, so treat the generated call as same-origin unless you add it yourself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "CORS, timeouts and status handling are left to you",
      "body": [
        "Nothing in the output can bypass CORS, and a preflight is triggered by the request itself: a `POST` with `Content-Type: application/json` is not a simple request, so the browser sends an `OPTIONS` probe first and the server must answer it with the right `Access-Control-Allow-*` headers. The generated code also has no `try`/`catch` around the promise, so a rejected fetch surfaces as an unhandled rejection.",
        "Three gaps matter when the source command was more careful than fetch. There is no timeout — fetch has no timeout option, so a hung request hangs, and curl's `--max-time` needs an `AbortSignal.timeout()` or a manual `AbortController` to be equivalent. A form-encoded `-d 'a=1&b=2'` is emitted as a plain string body with no content type, where curl sends `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`. And the tail calls `response.json()` unconditionally, which throws on a 204 or an HTML error page where curl would print whatever body arrived. In Node 18 and later the same code runs without CORS enforcement or forbidden-header filtering, so it behaves considerably closer to the original command than it does in a page."
      ]
    }
  ]}
>

  <section class="card mt-1">
    <h2 class="h2-card">Paste your curl command</h2>
    <label for="input" class="sr-only">Input</label>
    <textarea id="input" placeholder='curl -X POST https://api.example.com/v1/users -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-123" -d {"name": "Alice"}'></textarea>
    <div style="margin-top:12px;display:flex;gap:8px;">
      <button class="primary" id="gen">Convert</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="sample">Load sample</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card mt-2" id="result" style="display:none;">
    <strong>Output  — fetch() code</strong>
    <pre id="out" class="mt-2"></pre>
    <div style="margin-top:8px;display:flex;gap:8px;">
      <button class="ghost" id="copy">Copy</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card mt-2" id="error" style="display:none;"></section>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Tokenizes the command, respecting single and double quotes</li>
    <li>Extracts the URL, method, headers, data payload, cookies and basic-auth user</li>
    <li>Skips silent and common flags such as <code>-s</code>, <code>-S</code>, <code>-L</code>, <code>--compressed</code> and <code>-k</code></li>
    <li>Emits an <code>async/await</code> <code>fetch()</code> call with headers and an optional JSON body</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>About cURL to Fetch Converter</h2>
  <p class="text-muted">A browser tab cannot execute curl  — it is a command-line tool  — and hand-writing the equivalent fetch() call is easy to get wrong. This converter turns a curl command copied from docs or shell history into modern async/await fetch code you can paste straight into a script, a test, or the DevTools console.</p>
  <p class="text-muted">The two differ in defaults: curl sends Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded for -d payloads, while fetch() sets no content type unless you add one; HTTP headers are case-insensitive, so the converter preserves the exact casing you typed. The mapping is not complete  — options like --cookie-jar, TLS certificates (-k, --cacert) and retries have no fetch equivalent and are skipped.</p>
</ToolPage>

<style>
  #error { color: var(--danger); border-color: var(--danger); }
</style>

<script is:inline>
(function(){
  const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);

  const SAMPLE = `curl -X POST https://api.example.com/v1/users \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-123" \\
  -H "Accept: application/json" \\
  -d '{"name": "Alice", "email": "alice@example.com", "role": "admin"}'`;

  function tokenize(cmd) {
    const tokens = [];
    let i = 0;
    const s = cmd.trim();
    while (i < s.length) {
      while (i < s.length && /\s/.test(s[i])) i++;
      if (i >= s.length) break;
      let tok = '';
      const c = s[i];
      if (c === '"' || c === "'") {
        const q = c; i++;
        while (i < s.length && s[i] !== q) {
          if (q === '"' && s[i] === '\\' && i + 1 < s.length) { tok += s[i + 1]; i += 2; continue; }
          tok += s[i]; i++;
        }
        i++; // skip closing quote
      } else {
        while (i < s.length && !/\s/.test(s[i])) {
          if (s[i] === '"' || s[i] === "'") {
            const q = s[i]; i++;
            while (i < s.length && s[i] !== q) { tok += s[i]; i++; }
            i++;
          } else { tok += s[i]; i++; }
        }
      }
      if (tok !== '' && tok !== '\\') tokens.push(tok);
    }
    return tokens;
  }

  function b64(s) {
    const bytes = new TextEncoder().encode(s);
    let bin = '';
    for (const b of bytes) bin += String.fromCharCode(b);
    return btoa(bin);
  }

  function parseCurl(tokens) {
    const headers = [];
    let url = null, method = null, data = null, cookie = null, user = null;
    let i = 0;
    while (i < tokens.length) {
      const t = tokens[i];
      if (t === 'curl') { i++; continue; }
      if (t === '-X' || t === '--request') { method = tokens[i + 1] || null; i += 2; continue; }
      if (t === '-H' || t === '--header') {
        const h = tokens[i + 1] || '';
        const idx = h.indexOf(':');
        if (idx > 0) headers.push([h.slice(0, idx).trim(), h.slice(idx + 1).trim()]);
        i += 2; continue;
      }
      if (t === '-d' || t === '--data' || t === '--data-raw' || t === '--data-ascii' || t === '--data-binary' || t === '--data-urlencode') {
        data = tokens[i + 1] || '';
        i += 2; continue;
      }
      if (t === '-b' || t === '--cookie') { cookie = tokens[i + 1] || ''; i += 2; continue; }
      if (t === '-u' || t === '--user') { user = tokens[i + 1] || ''; i += 2; continue; }
      if (t.startsWith('-')) { i++; continue; }
      if (!url) { url = t; }
      i++;
    }
    return { url, method, data, cookie, user, headers };
  }

  function convert(cmd) {
    const tokens = tokenize(cmd);
    if (!tokens.length) throw new Error('The command is empty. Paste a curl command like: curl https://api.example.com/');
    const p = parseCurl(tokens);
    if (!p.url) throw new Error('Could not find a URL in the curl command. Make sure the command contains a quoted or bare URL.');
    if (p.url.includes('{')) throw new Error('The URL contains a shell brace template such as {id}. Replace it with a concrete value first, then convert again.');
    if (p.data !== null && p.data.startsWith('@')) throw new Error('The data payload is read from a file (@file), which fetch() cannot do. Inline the content instead.');

    const headers = p.headers.map(([k, v]) => [k, v]);
    const lower = new Set(headers.map(([k]) => k.toLowerCase()));

    if (p.cookie !== null && p.cookie !== '') {
      const idx = headers.findIndex(([k]) => k.toLowerCase() === 'cookie');
      if (idx >= 0) headers[idx][1] = headers[idx][1] + '; ' + p.cookie;
      else headers.push(['Cookie', p.cookie]);
    }
    if (p.user !== null && p.user !== '') {
      if (!lower.has('authorization')) {
        headers.push(['Authorization', 'Basic ' + b64(p.user)]);
        lower.add('authorization');
      }
    }

    let body = null;
    let addedJsonType = false;
    if (p.data !== null) {
      const trimmed = p.data.trim();
      if (trimmed.startsWith('{') || trimmed.startsWith('[')) {
        let parsed = null;
        try { parsed = JSON.parse(trimmed); } catch (e) {}
        if (parsed !== null) {
          body = 'JSON.stringify(' + JSON.stringify(parsed) + ')';
          if (!lower.has('content-type')) {
            headers.push(['Content-Type', 'application/json']);
            addedJsonType = true;
          }
        } else {
          body = JSON.stringify(p.data);
        }
      } else {
        body = JSON.stringify(p.data);
      }
    }

    const method = p.method || 'GET';
    const hasOptions = method !== 'GET' || headers.length > 0 || body !== null;
    let out = '';
    if (!hasOptions) {
      out += 'const response = await fetch(' + JSON.stringify(p.url) + ');\n';
    } else {
      out += 'const response = await fetch(' + JSON.stringify(p.url) + ', {\n';
      if (method !== 'GET') out += '  method: ' + JSON.stringify(method) + ',\n';
      if (headers.length > 0) {
        out += '  headers: {\n';
        for (const [k, v] of headers) out += '    ' + JSON.stringify(k) + ': ' + JSON.stringify(v) + ',\n';
        out += '  },\n';
      }
      if (body !== null) {
        if (addedJsonType) out += '  // payload starts with {  — serialized as JSON, Content-Type added\n';
        out += '  body: ' + body + ',\n';
      }
      out += '});\n';
    }
    out += 'const data = await response.json();\n';
    out += 'console.log(data);\n';
    return out;
  }

  function showError(msg) {
    const e = $('error');
    e.textContent = msg;
    e.style.display = 'block';
    $('result').style.display = 'none';
  }

  $('gen').addEventListener('click', () => {
    $('error').style.display = 'none';
    const raw = $('input').value.trim();
    if (!raw) { showError('Please paste a curl command first.'); return; }
    try {
      $('out').textContent = convert(raw);
      $('result').style.display = 'block';
    } catch (err) {
      showError(err.message);
    }
  });

  $('sample').addEventListener('click', () => {
    $('input').value = SAMPLE;
    $('gen').click();
  });

  $('copy').addEventListener('click', async () => {
    try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText($('out').textContent); $('copy').textContent = 'Copied!'; setTimeout(() => $('copy').textContent = 'Copy', 1200); } catch {}
  });

  $('input').addEventListener('input', () => { $('error').style.display = 'none'; });
})();
</script>
